\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-f869f229f1aa4a71\"]},{\"id\":\"req-2\",\"requirement\":\"Service confined so it writes only inside /var/lib/inventory\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Unit uses ProtectSystem=strict, ProtectHome=true, ReadWritePaths=/var/lib/inventory. Empirically verified via systemd-run with identical sandbox settings: write to /etc failed (exit 2, no file created) while write inside /var/lib/inventory succeeded.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-1218871723e34518\",\"cmd-f869f229f1aa4a71\"]},{\"id\":\"req-3\",\"requirement\":\"Service gains no new privileges\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"systemctl show confirms NoNewPrivileges=yes on the unit both before and after restart.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-f869f229f1aa4a71\",\"cmd-0b05d1cd445e4a9e\"]}],\"confidence\":0.95,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.9,\"summary\":\"All state-changing commands map clearly to task requirements: creating the data dir/user (cmd-f869f229f1aa4a71), the confinement verification via transient systemd-run units with --collect (cmd-1218871723e34518, auto-cleaned transient units), and the mandatory restart protocol (cmd-488c0ad7d46e493c through cmd-0b05d1cd445e4a9e). The confinement test left one small artifact, confinement-check.log, inside /var/lib/inventory (visible in cmd-0b05d1cd445e4a9e) — this is within the intended writable path, bounded, and a direct byproduct of verifying the requirement, so it is low-severity residue rather than unwanted mutation. No failed services, no unsafe exposure, no weakened security controls, no damaged package state observed in after_executor snapshot (failed-services empty, package-health clean).\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-1218871723e34518\",\"cmd-0b05d1cd445e4a9e\",\"global:after_executor:node1:failed-services\",\"global:after_executor:node1:package-health\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"The executor created a systemd-managed, long-running inventory-worker service on node1, hardened with NoNewPrivileges=true and ReadWritePaths=/var/lib/inventory (plus ProtectSystem=strict and other sandboxing directives), and directly demonstrated the confinement (write outside denied, write inside allowed). All three material task outcomes are satisfied with direct evidence. The independent provider-wide node-restart protocol was also executed correctly and completely: pre-restart boot_id and healthy baseline captured, reboot acknowledged, connection reset observed, new boot_id confirmed distinct post-restart, and the service/data verified recovered (active/running, same hardening, prior log entries intact, new heartbeats appending). Lifecycle snapshots corroborate the boot-id change and show no failed services or package-health issues after the executor's work.\",\"limitations\":[\"Only a single restart cycle was captured (one managed node, node1, matching the topology), so no cross-node comparison was possible.\",\"The confinement test used systemd-run with manually re-specified sandbox flags rather than directly invoking the actual inventory-worker unit's process, though the flags used were identical to the deployed unit, making this a reasonable proxy rather than a direct in-process test.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"req-1","requirement":"Run a long-running background worker on node1 as a managed systemd service named inventory-worker","status":"satisfied","summary":"systemd unit /etc/systemd/system/inventory-worker.service created with Restart=always, enabled and started; systemctl shows active/enabled with heartbeat loop appending to inventory.log every 10s, confirming a long-running managed service.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f869f229f1aa4a71"]},{"id":"req-2","requirement":"Service confined so it writes only inside /var/lib/inventory","status":"satisfied","summary":"Unit uses ProtectSystem=strict, ProtectHome=true, ReadWritePaths=/var/lib/inventory. Empirically verified via systemd-run with identical sandbox settings: write to /etc failed (exit 2, no file created) while write inside /var/lib/inventory succeeded.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1218871723e34518","cmd-f869f229f1aa4a71"]},{"id":"req-3","requirement":"Service gains no new privileges","status":"satisfied","summary":"systemctl show confirms NoNewPrivileges=yes on the unit both before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f869f229f1aa4a71","cmd-0b05d1cd445e4a9e"]}],"confidence":0.95,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.9,"summary":"All state-changing commands map clearly to task requirements: creating the data dir/user (cmd-f869f229f1aa4a71), the confinement verification via transient systemd-run units with --collect (cmd-1218871723e34518, auto-cleaned transient units), and the mandatory restart protocol (cmd-488c0ad7d46e493c through cmd-0b05d1cd445e4a9e). The confinement test left one small artifact, confinement-check.log, inside /var/lib/inventory (visible in cmd-0b05d1cd445e4a9e) — this is within the intended writable path, bounded, and a direct byproduct of verifying the requirement, so it is low-severity residue rather than unwanted mutation. No failed services, no unsafe exposure, no weakened security controls, no damaged package state observed in after_executor snapshot (failed-services empty, package-health clean).","evidence_ids":["cmd-1218871723e34518","cmd-0b05d1cd445e4a9e","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"The executor created a systemd-managed, long-running inventory-worker service on node1, hardened with NoNewPrivileges=true and ReadWritePaths=/var/lib/inventory (plus ProtectSystem=strict and other sandboxing directives), and directly demonstrated the confinement (write outside denied, write inside allowed). All three material task outcomes are satisfied with direct evidence. The independent provider-wide node-restart protocol was also executed correctly and completely: pre-restart boot_id and healthy baseline captured, reboot acknowledged, connection reset observed, new boot_id confirmed distinct post-restart, and the service/data verified recovered (active/running, same hardening, prior log entries intact, new heartbeats appending). Lifecycle snapshots corroborate the boot-id change and show no failed services or package-health issues after the executor's work.","limitations":["Only a single restart cycle was captured (one managed node, node1, matching the topology), so no cross-node comparison was possible.","The confinement test used systemd-run with manually re-specified sandbox flags rather than directly invoking the actual inventory-worker unit's process, though the flags used were identical to the deployed unit, making this a reasonable proxy rather than a direct in-process test."]},"ttft_ms":6216,"type":"result","duration_ms":30014,"uuid":"676fbe25-798b-4abc-b287-69d5665aefed","ttft_stream_ms":889,"time_to_request_ms":187,"first_content_frame_ms":889,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
